l checkpoints and validation reports. We will automate the generation of these logs during testing.\n    Why: It transforms static compliance paperwork into a scientific asset that tracks the intellectual evolution of our systems. (92 words) - *Good.*\n\n    *Refining Proposal 3:*\n    Title: Algorithmic Interpretability for Post-Market Monitoring\n    What: This is a new research initiative focusing on creating interpretable logs that translate raw system events into human-comprehensible risk indicators. The goal is to bridge the gap between binary logs and semantic understanding.\n    How: The team will investigate novel methods for event aggregation and anomaly detection within high-dimensional log data to identify substantial modifications automatically. We will publish these findings in top-tier AI safety venues.\n    Why: This pushes the knowledge frontier of AI observability while directly addressing the legal requirements for monitoring high-risk systems. (91 words) - *Good.*",
