        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The lab must transition from a flexible research posture to a rigorous industrial compliance framework regarding data provenance and system telemetry. We cannot treat logging as an optional debugging tool; it must become a core engineering requirement integrated into the development lifecycle. Failure to implement these traceability measures risks severe financial penalties and could bar our systems from the European market entirely. Our priority is now the institutionalization of accountability through automated record-keeping.\",\n  \"stance\": 35,\n  \"proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Automated Compliance Logging Framework\",\n      \"what\": \"A standardized middleware layer integrated into all high-risk AI pipelines to automatically capture event logs and system telemetry. This ensures that every operational action is recorded chronologically.\",\n      \"how\": \"We will develop a set of universal API wrappers that log timestamps, input hashes, and state transitions to a secure, tamper-proof database. These tools will be mandatory for all production-ready models.\",\n      \"why\": \"This ensures systematic compliance with Article 12(1) without relying on the inconsistent diligence of individual researchers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Living Technical Documentation Pipeline\",\n      \"what\": \"A dynamic documentation system that automatically links model versions to training data, validation results, and risk assessments. It replaces static reports with a live traceability matrix.\",\n      \"how\": \"We will implement a version-control system for datasets and hyperparameters that auto-generates compliance reports during the CI/CD process. This pipeline will sync directly with our research repositories.\",\n      \"why\": \"This minimizes the administrative burden of keeping technical documentation up to date throughout the lifetime of the AI system.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Human-in-th