        "content": "{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The lab must transition from ad-hoc experimentation to a structured compliance-by-design architecture for all high-risk prototypes. We need to implement standardized logging frameworks early in the development lifecycle so that traceability does not become a bottleneck during final validation. By automating record-keeping at the infrastructure level, we can maintain our prototyping speed while meeting legal mandates. This ensures technical viability without compromising our agility.\",\n  \"stance\": 30,\n  \"proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Unified Compliance Logging Middleware\",\n      \"what\": \"A universal API layer for all high-risk prototypes that automatically captures event timestamps and system states. It standardizes how telemetry is collected across different AI architectures.\",\n      \"how\": \"We will develop a lightweight Python library integrated into our core ML pipeline that pipes logs to a centralized, immutable database.\",\n      \"why\": \"It removes the burden of manual logging from researchers and ensures consistent compliance across diverse projects.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Automated Technical Documentation Pipeline\",\n      \"what\": \"A toolchain that auto-generates required technical documentation by pulling metadata directly from training scripts and dataset manifests. This replaces manual reporting with live data.\",\n      \"how\": \"We will implement a system using MLflow or similar tracking tools to capture hyperparameters, data versions, and validation metrics in real-time.\",\n      \"why\": \"It reduces the administrative overhead of record-keeping, allowing engineers to focus on prototyping rather than paperwork.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Traceability Validation Sandbox\",\n      \"what\": \"A dedicated testing environment that simulates specific logging requirements for Annex III systems to verify traceability before deployment. It serves as a pre-cer