ty can use, positioning the lab as a leader.\n        *   Title: Open Standard for Regulatory Traceability Benchmarks\n        *   What: The development of an open-source specification and test suite to evaluate if AI logging meets Article 12 standards.\n        *   How: We will collaborate with other R&D institutions to define \"appropriate traceability\" and publish the resulting benchmark.\n        *   Why: It expands our scientific impact by shaping how the global research community implements EU AI Act requirements.\n\n    *   Check constraints:\n        *   Reasoning 3-5 sentences? Yes.\n        *   Stance score (0-100)? Yes.\n        *   Exactly 3 proposals? Yes.\n        *   Distinct/concrete? Yes (Tooling, Research on failure modes, Open Standard).\n        *   Title (<10 words), What (1-2 sentences), How (1-2 sentences), Why (1 sentence)? Yes.\n        *   Length per proposal 60-110 words?\n            *   Prop 1: ~65 words.\n            *   Prop 2: ~70 words.\n            *   Prop 3: ~75 words.\n        *   No bullet lists inside fields? Yes. Plain prose? Yes.\n        *   Role maintained? (Researcher focused on frontier/impact). Yes.",
