        "content": "{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The lab must immediately integrate systematic logging and documentation protocols into its development lifecycle for all projects classified as high-risk. Since these requirements are prescriptive, failure to implement them creates an existential legal risk and damages our reputation with EU partners. We should treat compliance not as a post-hoc addition but as a core engineering constraint of the R&D process.\",\n  \"stance\": 25,\n  \"proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Universal High-Risk Logging Architecture\",\n      \"what\": \"A standardized software module integrated into all high-risk AI pipelines to automatically capture event logs and timestamps. It provides a unified way to record system behavior.\",\n      \"how\": \"Engineers will develop a centralized API that records system inputs, output matches, and user interactions across different R&D projects. This API will feed into a secure, immutable database.\",\n      \"why\": \"This ensures consistent compliance with Article 12(1) without forcing every researcher to build their own logging system from scratch.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Live Compliance Documentation Pipeline\",\n      \"what\": \"A dynamic version-control system for technical documentation that tracks algorithms, training data, and risk assessments in real-time. It replaces static reports with living documents.\",\n      \"how\": \"We will implement a mandatory documentation template integrated into our Git workflow that requires updates before any model deployment. These templates will be automatically compiled into regulatory dossiers.\",\n      \"why\": \"It satisfies Recital 71 by maintaining up-to-date records essential for regulatory audits and traceability throughout the system lifetime.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"High-Risk AI Classification Audit\",\n      \"what\": \"A formal internal review process to categorize all current and planned projects based on EU AI Act risk tiers. This serves as our institutional compliance map.\",\n      \"how\": \"Legal and technical leads will map our R&D portfolio against Annex III to identify which systems trigger Article 12 mandates. This audit will be repeated quarterly for new research paths.\",\n      \"why\": \"This prevents the catastrophic failure of deploying a high-risk system that lacks required logging capabilities, protecting institutional survival.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
