        "content": "{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The lab must transition from a pure research mindset to one of rigorous industrial traceability. Since Article 12 mandates that logging capabilities be technically integrated, we can no longer treat observability as an optional post-hoc addition. Failure to bake these requirements into our architecture will result in non-compliant products, risking heavy fines and market exclusion. We must standardize our record-keeping to ensure institutional survival and maintain our reputation for regulatory excellence.\",\n  \"stance\": 30,\n  \"proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Standardized Logging Framework for High-Risk Systems\",\n      \"what\": \"A universal internal API and data schema for event logging across all high-risk projects.\",\n      \"how\": \"Engineers will develop a shared software library that captures timestamps, input hashes, and system states by default during the development phase.\",\n      \"why\": \"This prevents fragmented implementation and ensures consistency for regulatory audits to protect our market reputation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Dynamic Technical Documentation Lifecycle Management\",\n      \"what\": \"A new protocol for keeping technical documentation updated in real-time throughout the AI system's lifetime.\",\n      \"how\": \"We will integrate automated documentation tools directly into our version control systems to sync code changes with capability disclosures.\",\n      \"why\": \"It fulfills Recital 71's requirement for up-to-date information, ensuring institutional survival during potential EU inspections.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Biometric Traceability Module for Identification Systems\",\n      \"what\": \"A specialized logging tool tailored specifically for systems falling under Annex III point 1(a).\",\n      \"how\": \"We will implement a secure, immutable ledger that records the specific reference database used and identifies human verifiers for every