cture/Tooling (The \"Standardized Wrapper\").* Create a middleware or library that handles logging automatically for all high-risk projects.\n        *   Title: Unified Compliance Logging Framework\n        *   What: A standardized internal software library that automates event recording and timestamping across all AI models.\n        *   How: We will assign a small engineering team to build an API wrapper that integrates with our existing compute clusters and databases.\n        *   Why: This prevents individual researchers from wasting funding on bespoke logging solutions for every project.\n\n    *   *Proposal 2: Process/Governance (The \"Audit Trail\").* Establish a protocol for documenting the human side of verification.\n        *   Title: Human-in-the-Loop Verification Protocol\n        *   What: A formalized administrative process to track and log which natural persons verified high-risk system results.\n        *   How: We will implement a digital signature system integrated into our model evaluation dashboards to capture auditor identities.\n        *   Why: It ensures strict compliance with Article 12(3)(d) without disrupting the scientific workflow.\n\n    *   *Proposal 3: Strategic Shift/New Research (The \"Efficient Logging\" angle).* Since we have to do it, let's make it a research goal to do it *efficiently* so it doesn't slow down our systems.\n        *   Title: Low-Overhead Telemetry Research Project\n        *   What: A targeted R&D effort to develop high-performance logging methods that minimize computational latency and storage costs.\n        *   How: Researchers will explore compressed event streaming and asynchronous logging architectures specifically for large-scale AI models.\n        *   Why: This turns a regulatory burden into a scientific advantage by improving our infrastructure efficiency.\n\n    *   Reasoning: 3-5 sentences? Yes.\n    *   Number (0-100)? Yes (25).\n    *   Exactly 3 proposals? Yes.\n    *   Title max 10 words? Yes.\n