hift, not a pivot in research direction. Let's go with 25.\n\n    *   *Proposal 1: Infrastructure/Tooling.* Create a standardized logging library for high-risk AI pipelines to ensure automatic compliance across all projects.\n    *   *Proposal 2: Scientific Methodology.* Research into \"Privacy-Preserving Logging.\" Since logs might contain sensitive input data (Art 12(3)(c)), we need a way to log without violating GDPR or security. This is actual R&D.\n    *   *Proposal 3: Documentation/Governance.* A systematic framework for \"Dynamic Technical Documentation\" that updates in real-time as the model evolves, rather than static PDFs.\n\n    *   *Refining Proposal 1:*\n        *   Title: Unified Compliance Logging Framework\n        *   What: A modular software library that automatically captures system events and metadata required by Article 12.\n        *   How: We will develop an API-driven logging wrapper to be integrated into all high-risk model training and deployment pipelines.\n        *   Why: This removes the manual burden from researchers while ensuring total regulatory traceability. (Words check: ~50 words... needs to be 60-110).\n        *   *Expansion:* Add more detail on \"How\" and \"What\".\n\n    *   *Refining Proposal 2:*\n        *   Title: Privacy-Preserving Traceability Research\n        *   What: A research project investigating cryptographic methods to log input data without exposing raw sensitive information.\n        *   How: We will explore secure multi-party computation and zero-knowledge proofs to verify log integrity without sacrificing privacy.\n        *   Why: This transforms a compliance burden into a contribution to the knowledge frontier of secure AI. (Words check: ~60 words).\n\n    *   *Refining Proposal 3:*\n        *   Title: Automated Living Technical Documentation System\n        *   What: An integrated system that maps model versioning and dataset changes directly to the required EU technical documentation.\n        *   How: