uing because:\n- It directly implements a core Art 12(1) requirement\n- The automated nature reduces compliance risk\n- Version control of inputs supports traceability\n- It's architecturally sound (middleware layer, not ad-hoc scripts)\n- The \"seamless audit trail\" framing aligns with the regulation's traceability purpose\n\nBut it's not a 90+ because of the gaps in covering the full lifetime and specific event categories. I'd say it's a strong proposal that needs scoping work to ensure it covers Art 12(2) and (3), but as stated, it addresses the core automatic logging requirement well.\n\nI'll approve it with a promise score reflecting its strong alignment but acknowledging the scope gaps. Maybe around 78-82? It's clearly aligned with my domain, architecturally sound for compliance purposes, but incomplete in covering the full regulatory surface. I'll go with 80.\n",
