tion) is sound, implementable, and high-value for R&D velocity.\n\nI'd lean toward approving this. It's technically viable, buildable quickly as a prototype, addresses a real friction point in our development cycle, and leverages infrastructure we likely already have. The promise score: it's not a moonshot, the technical path is clear, but there are meaningful gaps between \"auto-extract metadata\" and \"fully comprehensive compliance documentation.\" I'd put this around 72-78 — technically very doable, high prototyping value, but the \"comprehensive\" claim sets expectations that the prototype alone won't fully meet.\n\nI'll go with approve at 75.\n",
